WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.937
Step five runs the sync.

2
00:00:01.937 --> 00:00:06.798
The dry run says create for the error
reporting policy, which isn't in the tenant,

3
00:00:06.798 --> 00:00:10.313
and no change for sign-in and
power, which already matches.

4
00:00:10.313 --> 00:00:13.774
Then the apply says created,
and both exit zero.

5
00:00:13.774 --> 00:00:17.241
The sync record shows the
scope the apply asked for,

6
00:00:17.241 --> 00:00:19.387
read-write, and the I D it created.

7
00:00:19.387 --> 00:00:23.530
Ask for a cloud name the
script doesn't know, U S gov,

8
00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:28.501
and it exits one: the cloud must be
G C C, global, G C C High or D O D.

9
00:00:28.501 --> 00:00:31.712
Step six breaks something on purpose.

10
00:00:31.712 --> 00:00:34.909
Change the hibernate
value in one library file,

11
00:00:34.909 --> 00:00:38.925
and the dry run exits two, with
a drift that names the setting.

12
00:00:38.925 --> 00:00:41.468
Run it with apply, and it still exits two,

13
00:00:41.468 --> 00:00:45.363
and nothing is created, not even
the error reporting policy.

14
00:00:45.363 --> 00:00:46.699
Put the value back.

15
00:00:46.699 --> 00:00:49.975
Step seven runs the tests: forty-six pass.

16
00:00:49.975 --> 00:00:52.180
Step eight deletes the out folder.
